Q. What is the architecture of SAP CPI -- imp
A. SAP CPI follows a multiple layer architecture built on cloud-native technologies , enabling seamless integration
 bw SAP and non SAP system

 layers :

 1. connectivity layer : (Adapting different systems)
 -> support multiple protocols :  HTTP, SOAP, JMS, AS2 , etc.
 -> use cloud connectors for secure on-premise integration
 -> provides per-package adapter for sap and third party applications.

 2.Process Layer :  (Apache camel and message routing)
 -> based on apache camel (integration framework)
 -> Handles message Transformation & routing using
   splitters, routers, aggregators , filters, and enrichers
   mapping (graphical , xslt , message mapping , Groovy , java script)

 3.Security layer : (data protection & authentication)
 -> uses OAuth 2.o , SAML , Basic Auth , and TLS for Authentication
 -> Supports data masking & encryption for sensitive data
 -> manages secure credential storage via security material

 4.Monitoring and management layer : (operations and analytics)
 -> message tracking and logs via cpi web ui
 -> message monitoring and alerts via SAP cloud ALM
 -> integration content management for deploying and configuring iflows

 5.persistence and storage layer (Data handling)
 -> uses data stores for temporary message storage.
 -> support jms queue for asynchronous processing.
 -> allows externalizing configurations via value mapping & parameters.
